Setup Instructions

Follow these steps to set up your environment and get started:

1. Install Python
If you don’t have Python installed, download and install it from [python.org](https://www.python.org/).

2. Set Up a Virtual Environment
A virtual environment helps keep your project dependencies isolated. Run the following commands:

```bash
# Create a virtual environment
python3 -m venv myenv (you should write this in terminal)

# Activate the virtual environment (you should write this in terminal)
>On macOS/Linux:
source myenv/bin/activate
>On Windows:
myenv\Scripts\activate
```

3. Install Required Packages
Install the necessary Python packages using `pip`: (Google PIP; it's very easy. We have also explained in theory in our course- Chapter 1)

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt (we have a list of all commonly used modules, libs, framework, and packages in the folder in a txt file)
```

4. Verify Installation
Check if everything is set up correctly:

```bash
python3 -c "import django; print(django.__version__)"
python3 -c "import pyttsx3; print(pyttsx3.init())"
```
